# Story 63: Loop Detection & Last-Prompt-Wins (45s)
# Hook: Runaway agents get stopped, and a new prompt always interrupts the old one.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-063-loop-detection-last-prompt-wins.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Runaway agents get stopped, and a new prompt always interrupts the old one.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh and drop into prompt mode.

[00:08.0 --> 00:20.0]
Give the agent a big task. The orchestrator watches a sliding window of twenty tool calls as it works.

[00:20.0 --> 00:34.0]
Change your mind mid-thought. Send a new prompt and the in-flight LLM call is cancelled -- last prompt wins.

[00:34.0 --> 00:42.0]
And if the agent repeats the same tool call three times, loop detection blocks it so it can never spin forever.

[00:42.0 --> 00:45.0]
Safe by design: no infinite loops, always interruptible.

